    "notes": "Inspected all 12 views. The compound-lever linkage is modelled as separate plates and pins rather than a fused blob, which holds up in the top and bottom views. Rust and paint loss are consistent between front and back; 3.4k tris is excellent for the silhouette. Clay shows clean, closed jaws.",
    "limitations": [
      "Very thin in the side-on views, as a real bolt cutter is; not a framing defect.",
      "Handles are closed, so the tool cannot be posed open without editing."
    ],
